  "notes": "Drawn from the right side (N845MH, 2017-07-31, flipped) read by hand: no measured 767-400 shape, so positions are shares of the length (within about 0.02) and heights through sin(y·90°) from a centreline and radius read at mid-fuselage. The ribbon is art: its big masses only, the loop as a pink ellipse with a white inside, the strands straight; the swoosh's pink-to-red shading drawn flat. The left side (2017-04-09, 2024-02-25) shows the same layout; the right side's widget is aft of 'DELTA' as the standard's. The navy belly and fin are Delta's standard (copied). Still flying in it: Commons 2024-02-25; a November 2025 photo elsewhere (lead only). Fin re-measured 2026-11-26 on N572DT (A321neo, left, 2025-02-01) fitted to shapes/A21N.json and read in fin space: the upper facet reaches the leading edge (it had stopped short), the shaded facet meets the root at x 0.53-0.715 and the lower-right one at 0.8 (both had been drawn 0.06-0.09 aft), the navy Y's stem between them (the edges carried on a little past the root, as the paint runs onto the fairing). The fin's widget logo entry is gone: the areas are the widget, cropped by the fin's edges, and a widget mark centred on the fin drew a second, wrong triangle over them.",
  "history": "Delta's 'pink plane' since 2010 (a 757 before it); this design from 2015."
}
